## 🎤 11. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What is persistence?**  
A technique that allows software or an attacker to maintain access across restarts or sign-ins.

**Q2. Name three Windows persistence locations.**  
Startup folders, Run registry keys, and scheduled tasks. Windows services can also be used.

**Q3. Why investigate scheduled tasks?**  
They can execute programs automatically based on configured triggers.

**Q4. Is every unknown startup program malicious?**  
No. Validate its publisher, location, purpose, configuration, and behavior.

**Q5. Why inspect a service's executable path?**  
It helps establish what code the service runs and whether the location is expected.

**Q6. What should a SOC analyst do after finding a suspicious entry?**  
Preserve relevant evidence, correlate associated events, assess impact, and escalate according to incident response procedures.

